{
  "case_id": "CASE-009",
  "category": "vrp_population_local_search",
  "description": [
    "Problem and representation: A configurable vehicle-routing framework reads an instance and builds a population of solutions. Its input model includes vehicle capacity and customer pickup, delivery, and time-window fields; actual constraint behavior depends on the instance and configuration.\n\n",
    "Population loop: Initialize the population and apply local search, then select parent pairs. Crossover alternates whole non-overlapping routes from the parents and uses the configured insertion strategy to repair missing customers; disabling crossover copies the first parent. Locally improve children, replace population members, and update the best solution. Search operators and stopping settings are exposed through command-line parameters.\n\n",
    "Boundary: This entry describes the supplied configurable implementation, not a claim that every configuration reproduces a particular paper. Verify the chosen operators, instance encoding, capacity and time-window semantics, and coverage before migration. SRC/argparse.h has its own BSD 3-clause license in addition to the repository MIT license."
  ],
